  "description": "RITFIL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C63 H99 Fe7 Gd3 N25 O26,4(C2 H3 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.238-3.936 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.85-145.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd3Fe7(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)2(N3)6(mdea)7(PhCO2)4]·4MeCN·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
